(Relevant Material For Exams) Tj
T*
(100% Success Rate for Exams) Tj
T*
(100% Success Guarantee in Technology & Exam Assistance) Tj
T*
(Your Expertise Our Desire) Tj
T*
(CCNA Exam Syllabus and Topics) Tj
T*
(Exam Description:) Tj
T*
(CCNA Exam v1.0 \(CCNA 200-301\) is a 120-minute exam associated with the CCNA certification.) Tj
T*
(This exam tests a candidate's knowledge and skills related to network fundamentals, network) Tj
T*
(access, IP connectivity, IP services, security fundamentals, and automation and) Tj
T*
(programmability. The course, Implementing and Administering Cisco Solutions \(CCNA\), helps) Tj
T*
(candidates prepare for this exam.) Tj
T*
(20% 1.0 Network Fundamentals) Tj
T*
(1.1 Explain the role and function of network components) Tj
T*
(1.2 Describe characteristics of network topology architectures) Tj
T*
(1.3 Compare physical interface and cabling types) Tj
T*
(1.4 Identify interface and cable issues \(collisions, errors, mismatch duplex, and/or speed\)) Tj
T*
(1.5 Compare TCP to UDP) Tj
T*
(1.6 Configure and verify IPv4 addressing and subnetting) Tj
T*
(1.7 Describe the need for private IPv4 addressing) Tj
T*
(1.8 Configure and verify IPv6 addressing and prefix) Tj
T*
(1.9 Compare IPv6 address types) Tj
T*
(1.10 Verify IP parameters for Client OS \(Windows, Mac OS, Linux\)) Tj
T*
(1.11 Describe wireless principles) Tj
T*
(1.12 Explain virtualization fundamentals \(virtual machines\)) Tj
T*
(1.13 Describe switching concepts) Tj
T*
(20% 2.0 Network Access) Tj
T*
(2.1 Configure and verify VLANs \(normal range\) spanning multiple switches) Tj
T*
(2.2 Configure and verify interswitch connectivity) Tj
T*
(2.3 Configure and verify Layer 2 discovery protocols \(Cisco Discovery Protocol and LLDP\)) Tj
T*
(2.4 Configure and verify \(Layer 2/Layer 3\) EtherChannel \(LACP\)) Tj
T*
(2.5 Describe the need for and basic operations of Rapid PVST+ Spanning Tree Protocol and) Tj
T*
(identify basic operations) Tj
T*
(2.6 Compare Cisco Wireless Architectures and AP modes) Tj
T*
(2.7 Describe physical infrastructure connections of WLAN components \(AP, WLC, access/trunk) Tj
T*
(ports, and LAG\)) Tj
T*
(2.8 Describe AP and WLC management access connections \(Telnet, SSH, HTTP, HTTPS, console,) Tj
T*
(and TACACS+/RADIUS\)) Tj
T*
(2.9 Configure the components of a wireless LAN access for client connectivity using GUI only) Tj
T*
(such as WLAN creation, security settings, QoS profiles, and advanced WLAN settings) Tj
T*
(25% 3.0 IP Connectivity) Tj
T*
(3.1 Interpret the components of routing table) Tj
T*
(3.2 Determine how a router makes a forwarding decision by default) Tj
T*
(3.3 Configure and verify IPv4 and IPv6 static routing) Tj
T*
(3.4 Configure and verify single area OSPFv2) Tj
T*
(3.5 Describe the purpose of first hop redundancy protocol) Tj
T*
(10% 4.0 IP Services) Tj
T*
(4.1 Configure and verify inside source NAT using static and pools) Tj
T*
(4.2 Configure and verify NTP operating in a client and server mode) Tj
T*
ET
