T*
(4.5 Describe the use of syslog features including facilities and levels) Tj
T*
(4.6 Configure and verify DHCP client and relay) Tj
T*
(4.7 Explain the forwarding per-hop behavior \(PHB\) for QoS such as classification, marking,) Tj
T*
(queuing, congestion, policing, shaping) Tj
T*
(4.8 Configure network devices for remote access using SSH) Tj
T*
(4.9 Describe the capabilities and function of TFTP/FTP in the network) Tj
T*
(15% 5.0 Security Fundamentals) Tj
T*
(5.1 Define key security concepts \(threats, vulnerabilities, exploits, and mitigation) Tj
T*
(techniques\)) Tj
T*
(5.2 Describe security program elements \(user awareness, training, and physical access) Tj
T*
(control\)) Tj
T*
(5.3 Configure device access control using local passwords) Tj
T*
(5.4 Describe security password policies elements, such as management, complexity, and) Tj
T*
(password alternatives \(multifactor authentication, certificates, and biometrics\)) Tj
T*
(5.5 Describe remote access and site-to-site VPNs) Tj
T*
(5.6 Configure and verify access control lists) Tj
T*
(5.7 Configure Layer 2 security features \(DHCP snooping, dynamic ARP inspection, and port) Tj
T*
(security\)) Tj
T*
(5.8 Differentiate authentication, authorization, and accounting concepts) Tj
T*
(5.9 Describe wireless security protocols \(WPA, WPA2, and WPA3\)) Tj
T*
(5.10 Configure WLAN using WPA2 PSK using the GUI) Tj
T*
(10% 6.0 Automation and Programmability) Tj
T*
(6.1 Explain how automation impacts network management) Tj
T*
(6.2 Compare traditional networks with controller-based networking) Tj
T*
(6.3 Describe controller-based and software defined architectures \(overlay, underlay, and) Tj
T*
(fabric\)) Tj
T*
(6.4 Compare traditional campus device management with Cisco DNA Center enabled device) Tj
T*
(management) Tj
T*
(6.5 Describe characteristics of REST-based APIs \(CRUD, HTTP verbs, and data encoding\)) Tj
T*
(6.6 Recognize the capabilities of configuration management mechanisms Puppet, Chef, and) Tj
T*
(Ansible) Tj
T*
(6.7 Interpret JSON encoded data) Tj
T*
(FAQ) Tj
T*
(1. What is CCNA Certification and Why is it Important?) Tj
T*
(CCNA Certification is a professional certification that shows you have the skills and) Tj
T*
(knowledge to work with computer networks. It is important because it can help you get a job) Tj
T*
(in the IT industry and advance your career.) Tj
T*
(2. How Do I Prepare for the CCNA Certification Exam?) Tj
T*
(To prepare for the CCNA Certification exam, you should study the exam topics and practice) Tj
T*
(with sample questions. You can also take a CCNA course or use study materials like books and) Tj
T*
(online resources.) Tj
T*
(3. What Are the Benefits of CCNA Certification?) Tj
T*
(CCNA Certification can help you get a job in the IT industry, advance your career, and) Tj
T*
(increase your earning potential. It can also show employers that you have the skills and) Tj
T*
(knowledge to work with computer networks.) Tj
T*
(4. What is Covered in the CCNA Certification Exam?) Tj
T*
ET
