(16. What happens if I fail the CCNP Security exams?) Tj
T*
(If you fail a CCNP Security exam, you can retake the exam after a waiting period of five) Tj
T*
(calendar days. However, you will need to pay the exam fee again for each attempt. You can) Tj
T*
(take the exam up to three times in a 12-month period, after which you must wait for 12) Tj
T*
(months before attempting the exam again. If you fail the same exam three times within a) Tj
T*
(12-month period, you will need to wait for 12 months from the date of your last attempt) Tj
T*
(before you can retake the exam. Additionally, if you fail an exam, Cisco provides a score) Tj
T*
(report that identifies your strengths and weaknesses in the exam content. Use this feedback) Tj
T*
(to identify areas where you need to improve before retaking the exam. It's important to note) Tj
T*
(that earning a CCNP Security certification requires passing multiple exams, so if you fail) Tj
T*
(one exam, it may delay your progress towards earning the certification. Be sure to take) Tj
T*
(advantage of the resources available to help you prepare for the exam, such as study) Tj
T*
(materials and training courses, to increase your chances of passing on your next attempt.) Tj
T*
(17. How can I recertify for CCNP Security certification?) Tj
T*
(To recertify for CCNP Security certification, you must pass any 300-level Cisco) Tj
T*
(professional-level or Cisco specialist exam \(excluding Sales Specialist exams\), or pass a) Tj
T*
(current CCIE written exam. Additionally, you can also recertify by passing any Cisco) Tj
T*
(professional-level concentration exam or passing the Cisco Certified Architect \(CCAr\)) Tj
T*
(interview and board review. You can also recertify your CCNP Security certification by) Tj
T*
(earning a higher-level certification, such as the Cisco Certified Internetwork Expert \(CCIE\)) Tj
T*
(Security certification. If you earn a higher-level certification, it automatically) Tj
T*
(recertifies all lower-level certifications, including CCNP Security. Another option for) Tj
T*
(recertification is to complete the Cisco Continuing Education Program, which allows you to) Tj
T*
(earn Continuing Education Credits \(CECs\) through activities such as attending Cisco Live) Tj
T*
(events, completing online training courses, or participating in Cisco Learning Network study) Tj
T*
(groups. You can earn enough CECs to recertify your CCNP Security certification for an) Tj
T*
(additional three years. It's important to note that CCNP Security certification is valid for) Tj
T*
(three years, after which you must recertify to maintain your certification status. Be sure) Tj
T*
(to review the recertification options and requirements on the Cisco website to ensure that) Tj
T*
(you stay up to date with the latest recertification requirements.) Tj
T*
(18. What is the CCNP Security recertification policy?) Tj
T*
(The CCNP Security recertification policy requires that you recertify your certification) Tj
T*
(every three years to maintain your certification status. Failure to recertify will result in) Tj
T*
(the expiration of your certification and the loss of any associated benefits. To recertify) Tj
T*
(your CCNP Security certification, you must pass any 300-level Cisco professional-level or) Tj
T*
(Cisco specialist exam \(excluding Sales Specialist exams\), or pass a current CCIE written) Tj
T*
(exam. You can also recertify by passing any Cisco professional-level concentration exam or) Tj
T*
(passing the Cisco Certified Architect \(CCAr\) interview and board review. In addition to) Tj
T*
(exam-based recertification, you can also recertify through the Cisco Continuing Education) Tj
T*
(Program. This program allows you to earn Continuing Education Credits \(CECs\) through a) Tj
T*
(variety of activities, such as attending Cisco Live events, completing online training) Tj
T*
(courses, or participating in Cisco Learning Network study groups. You can earn enough CECs) Tj
T*
(to recertify your CCNP Security certification for an additional three years. It's important) Tj
T*
(to note that you must recertify before your certification expires to avoid a gap in your) Tj
T*
(certification status. If your certification expires, you will need to start the) Tj
T*
(certification process from the beginning and meet all current certification requirements. Be) Tj
T*
ET
