(Implementing and Operating Cisco Data Center Core Technologies v1.0 \(350-601\)) Tj
T*
(Exam Description:) Tj
T*
(Implementing and Operating Cisco Data Center Core Technologies v1.0 \(DCCOR 350-601\) is a) Tj
T*
(120-minute exam associated with the CCNP and CCIE Data Center Certifications. This exam) Tj
T*
(tests a candidate's knowledge of implementing core data center technologies including) Tj
T*
(network, compute, storage network, automation, and security. The course, Implementing Cisco) Tj
T*
(Data Center Core Technologies, helps candidates to prepare for this exam.) Tj
T*
(25% 1.0 Network) Tj
T*
(1.1 Apply routing protocols) Tj
T*
(1.2 Apply switching protocols such as RSTP+, LACP and vPC) Tj
T*
(1.3 Apply overlay protocols such as VXLAN EVPN and OTV) Tj
T*
(1.4 Apply ACI concepts) Tj
T*
(1.5 Analyze packet flow \(unicast, multicast, and broadcast\)) Tj
T*
(1.6 Analyze Cloud service and deployment models \(NIST 800-145\)) Tj
T*
(1.7 Describe software updates and their impacts) Tj
T*
(1.8 Implement network configuration management) Tj
T*
(1.9 Implement infrastructure monitoring such as NetFlow and SPAN) Tj
T*
(1.10 Explain network assurance concepts such as streaming telemetry) Tj
T*
(25% 2.0 Compute) Tj
T*
(2.1 Implement Cisco Unified Compute System Rack Servers) Tj
T*
(2.2 Implement Cisco Unified Compute System Blade Chassis) Tj
T*
