(3. What topics are covered in CCNP Service Provider Training?) Tj
T*
(CCNP Service Provider \(Cisco Certified Network Professional Service Provider\) Training is) Tj
T*
(designed to provide IT professionals with the advanced knowledge and skills required to) Tj
T*
(design, implement, and troubleshoot complex service provider networks. The program covers a) Tj
T*
(wide range of topics related to service provider networking, including:) Tj
T*
(1. IP routing technologies, including advanced routing protocols such as OSPF, BGP, and IS-) Tj
T*
(IS.) Tj
T*
(2. MPLS \(Multiprotocol Label Switching\) technologies, including MPLS Layer 3 VPNs, MPLS) Tj
T*
(Layer 2 VPNs, MPLS Traffic Engineering \(TE\), and MPLS multicast.) Tj
T*
(3. Quality of Service \(QoS\) technologies, including classification, marking, policing,) Tj
T*
(shaping, and congestion management.) Tj
T*
(4. Service Provider IPv6, including IPv6 addressing and routing, and transition technologies) Tj
T*
(such as Dual Stack and 6PE/6VPE.) Tj
T*
(5. VPN \(Virtual Private Network\) technologies, including site-to-site VPNs and remote access) Tj
T*
(VPNs.) Tj
T*
(6. Network security, including access control, firewall technologies, and intrusion) Tj
T*
(prevention systems.) Tj
T*
(7. Network management, including network monitoring, device management, and network) Tj
T*
(automation.) Tj
T*
(The training includes both theoretical and hands-on practical components to ensure that) Tj
T*
(candidates gain a deep understanding of service provider networking concepts and) Tj
T*
(technologies and can apply them to real-world scenarios. By completing CCNP Service Provider) Tj
T*
(Training, IT professionals can demonstrate their expertise in service provider networking) Tj
T*
(and advance their careers in the industry.) Tj
T*
