(30% 2.0 Infrastructure as Code) Tj
T*
(2.1 Create a scalable solution for infrastructure automation \(considering areas such as) Tj
T*
(network impact, risk, and tool selection\)) Tj
T*
(2.2 Build, manage, and operate a Python-based REST API with a web application framework) Tj
T*
(\(endpoints, HTTP request, and response\)) Tj
T*
(2.3 Build, manage, and operate a Python-based CLI application to use a REST API) Tj
T*
(2.4 Consume and use a new REST API, given the documentation) Tj
T*
(2.5 Create a RESTCONF or NETCONF payload based on a given YANG module, and interpret the) Tj
T*
(response) Tj
T*
(2.6 Create a NETCONF filter by using XPath) Tj
T*
(2.7 Configure network devices on an existing infrastructure by using NETCONF or RESTCONF,) Tj
T*
(given YANG analysis tools) Tj
T*
(2.8 Create and use a role by utilizing Ansible to manage infrastructure, given support) Tj
T*
(documentation) Tj
T*
(2.9 Use Terraform to statefully manage infrastructure, given support documentation) Tj
T*
(2.10 Create a basic Cisco NSO service package to meet given business and technical) Tj
T*
(requirements. The service would generate a network configuration on the target device) Tj
T*
(platforms using the "cisco-ios-cli" NED and be of type "python-and-template") Tj
T*
(25% 3.0 Network Programmability and Automation) Tj
T*
(3.1 Create, modify, and troubleshoot scripts by using Python libraries and SDK documentation) Tj
T*
(to automate against APIs \(ACI, AppDynamics, DNA Center, FDM, Intersight, IOS XE, Meraki,) Tj
T*
(NSO, Webex\)) Tj
T*
(3.2 Automate the configuration of a Cisco IOS XE network device \(based on a provided) Tj
T*
(architecture and configuration\), including these components:) Tj
T*
(3.3 Deploy an application on a Cisco IOS XE device by leveraging the technologies of Guest) Tj
T*
(Shell and application hosting) Tj
T*
(3.4 Modify and troubleshoot an automated test by using pyATS to meet requirements) Tj
T*
(3.5 Design a model-driven telemetry solution based on given business and technical) Tj
T*
(requirements by using gNMI dial-in, gRPC dial-out, and NETCONF dial-in) Tj
T*
(3.6 Create YANG model-driven telemetry subscriptions) Tj
T*
(10% 4.0 Containers) Tj
T*
(4.1 Create a Docker image \(including Dockerfile\)) Tj
T*
(4.2 Package and deploy a solution by using Docker Compose) Tj
T*
(4.3 Package and deploy a solution by using Kubernetes) Tj
T*
(4.4 Create, consume, and troubleshoot a Docker host and bridge-based networks and integrate) Tj
T*
(them with external networks) Tj
T*
(15% 5.0 Security) Tj
T*
(5.1 Leverage OWASP secure coding practices into all solutions to meet given requirements) Tj
T*
(5.2 Create a certificate signing request \(CSR\) by using OpenSSL; send CSR to a provided) Tj
T*
(certificate authority; and use the certificate to secure a web application) Tj
T*
(5.3 Use OAuth2+ to obtain an authentication token) Tj
T*
(5.4 Use a secret management system to secure an application) Tj
T*
(5.5 Use tokens, headers, and secrets to secure a REST API) Tj
T*
(FAQ) Tj
T*
(1. What is Devnet Expert Certification Training?) Tj
T*
(Devnet Expert Certification Training is an advanced course designed to provide professionals) Tj
T*
(with the skills and knowledge needed to design and develop complex applications built on) Tj
T*
(Cisco platforms. The course covers various topics, including advanced software development,) Tj
T*
