T*
(Exam Description:) Tj
T*
(Implementing and Operating Cisco Security Core Technologies v1.0 \(SCOR 350-701\) is a) Tj
T*
(120-minute exam associated with the CCNP and CCIE Security Certifications. This exam tests a) Tj
T*
(candidate's knowledge of implementing and operating core security technologies including) Tj
T*
(network security, cloud security, content security, endpoint protection and detection,) Tj
T*
(secure network access, visibility and enforcements. The course, Implementing and Operating) Tj
T*
(Cisco Security Core Technologies, helps candidates to prepare for this exam.) Tj
T*
(25% 1.0 Security Concepts) Tj
T*
(1.1 Explain common threats against on-premises and cloud environments) Tj
T*
(1.2 Compare common security vulnerabilities such as software bugs, weak and/or hardcoded) Tj
T*
(passwords, SQL injection, missing encryption, buffer overflow, path traversal, cross-site) Tj
T*
(scripting/forgery) Tj
T*
(1.3 Describe functions of the cryptography components such as hashing, encryption, PKI, SSL,) Tj
T*
(IPsec, NAT-T IPv4 for IPsec, pre-shared key and certificate based authorization) Tj
T*
(1.4 Compare site-to-site VPN and remote access VPN deployment types such as sVTI, IPsec,) Tj
T*
(Cryptomap, DMVPN, FLEXVPN including high availability considerations, and AnyConnect) Tj
T*
(1.5 Describe security intelligence authoring, sharing, and consumption) Tj
T*
(1.6 Explain the role of the endpoint in protecting humans from phishing and social) Tj
T*
(engineering attacks) Tj
T*
(1.7 Explain North Bound and South Bound APIs in the SDN architecture) Tj
T*
(1.8 Explain DNAC APIs for network provisioning, optimization, monitoring, and) Tj
T*
(troubleshooting) Tj
T*
(1.9 Interpret basic Python scripts used to call Cisco Security appliances APIs) Tj
T*
(20% 2.0 Network Security) Tj
T*
(2.1 Compare network security solutions that provide intrusion prevention and firewall) Tj
T*
(capabilities) Tj
T*
(2.2 Describe deployment models of network security solutions and architectures that provide) Tj
T*
(intrusion prevention and firewall capabilities) Tj
T*
(2.3 Describe the components, capabilities, and benefits of NetFlow and Flexible NetFlow) Tj
T*
(records) Tj
T*
(2.4 Configure and verify network infrastructure security methods \(router, switch, wireless\)) Tj
T*
(2.5 Implement segmentation, access control policies, AVC, URL filtering, and malware) Tj
T*
(protection) Tj
T*
(2.6 Implement management options for network security solutions such as intrusion prevention) Tj
T*
(and perimeter security \(Single vs. multidevice manager, in-band vs. out-ofband, CDP, DNS,) Tj
T*
(SCP, SFTP, and DHCP security and risks\)) Tj
T*
(2.7 Configure AAA for device and network access \(authentication and authorization, TACACS+,) Tj
T*
