T*
(taking. Cisco does not publicly disclose the exact passing score for each exam, as the score) Tj
T*
(is based on a complex statistical analysis of the questions and is subject to change.) Tj
T*
(However, Cisco provides a score report at the end of each exam that indicates whether you) Tj
T*
(passed or failed, as well as your overall score on the exam. In general, you can expect to) Tj
T*
(need a score of at least 70% to pass a CCNP Security exam. It's important to note that) Tj
T*
(passing the exam is only one step in earning your CCNP Security certification. You will also) Tj
T*
(need to meet other requirements, such as completing prerequisite exams and/or training) Tj
T*
(courses, in order to earn the certification. Be sure to review the certification) Tj
T*
(requirements on the Cisco website for full details.) Tj
T*
(16. What happens if I fail the CCNP Security exams?) Tj
T*
(If you fail a CCNP Security exam, you can retake the exam after a waiting period of five) Tj
T*
(calendar days. However, you will need to pay the exam fee again for each attempt. You can) Tj
T*
(take the exam up to three times in a 12-month period, after which you must wait for 12) Tj
T*
(months before attempting the exam again. If you fail the same exam three times within a) Tj
T*
(12-month period, you will need to wait for 12 months from the date of your last attempt) Tj
T*
