(10. What is the validity of CCNP Service Provider certification?) Tj
T*
(The CCNP Service Provider certification is valid for three years from the date of) Tj
T*
(certification. After this period, candidates must recertify to maintain their certification) Tj
T*
(status. Recertification can be achieved by passing any one of the following exams:) Tj
T*
(1. Pass any current CCNP-level exam or) Tj
T*
(2. Pass any current 642-XXX Professional-level or Cisco Specialist exam \(excluding Sales) Tj
T*
(Specialist exams or Meeting Place Specialist exams, Implementing Cisco Telepresence) Tj
T*
(Installations \(ITI\) exams, Cisco Leading Virtual Classroom Instruction exams, or any 650) Tj
T*
(online exams\).) Tj
T*
(Alternatively, candidates can also recertify by passing a current CCIE written exam or CCDE) Tj
T*
(written or practical exam.) Tj
T*
(It is important to note that recertification is necessary to maintain the validity of the) Tj
T*
(CCNP Service Provider certification. Failing to recertify before the certification) Tj
T*
(expiration date can result in the certification becoming inactive, which can impact job) Tj
T*
(opportunities and career growth.) Tj
T*
(In summary, the CCNP Service Provider certification is valid for three years, and candidates) Tj
T*
(must recertify to maintain their certification status. Recertification can be achieved by) Tj
T*
(passing certain exams or by passing a current CCIE or CCDE written or practical exam.) Tj
