(Implementing Cisco Collaboration Core Technologies v1.0 \(350-801\)) Tj
T*
(Exam Description:) Tj
T*
(Implementing Cisco Collaboration Core Technologies v1.0 \(CLCOR 350-801\) is a 120-minute exam) Tj
T*
(associated with the CCNP and CCIE Collaboration Certifications. This exam tests a) Tj
T*
(candidate's knowledge of implementing core collaboration technologies including) Tj
T*
(infrastructure and design, protocols, codecs, and endpoints, Cisco IOS XE gateway and media) Tj
T*
(resources, Call Control, QoS, and collaboration applications. The course, Implementing Cisco) Tj
T*
(Collaboration Core Technologies, helps candidates to prepare for this exam.) Tj
T*
(20% 1.0 Infrastructure and Design) Tj
T*
(1.1 Describe the key design elements of the following, pertaining to the Cisco Collaboration) Tj
T*
(architecture as described in the SRND/PA) Tj
T*
(1.2 Describe the purpose of Edge devices in the Cisco Collaboration architecture such as) Tj
T*
(Expressway and Cisco Unified Border Element) Tj
T*
(1.3 Configure these network components to support Cisco Collaboration solutions) Tj
T*
(1.4 Troubleshoot these network components in a Cisco Collaboration solution) Tj
T*
(1.5 Explain these components to support Cisco Collaboration solutions) Tj
T*
