(Exam Description:) Tj
T*
(The Cisco CCIE Security \(v6.0\) Practical Exam is an eight-hour, hands-on exam that requires) Tj
T*
(a candidate to plan, design, deploy, operate, and optimize network security solutions to) Tj
T*
(protect your network.) Tj
T*
(1. Perimeter Security and Intrusion Prevention \(20%\)) Tj
T*
(1.1 Deployment modes on Cisco ASA and Cisco FTD) Tj
T*
(1.2 Firewall features on Cisco ASA and Cisco FTD) Tj
T*
(1.3 Security features on Cisco IOS/IOS-XE) Tj
T*
(1.4 Cisco Firepower Management Center \(FMC\) features) Tj
T*
(1.5 NGIPS deployment modes) Tj
T*
(1.6 Next Generation Firewall \(NGFW\) features) Tj
T*
(1.7 Detect, and mitigate common types of attacks) Tj
T*
(1.8 Clustering/HA features on Cisco ASA and Cisco FTD) Tj
T*
(1.9 Policies and rules for traffic control on Cisco ASA and Cisco FTD) Tj
T*
(1.10 Routing protocols security on Cisco IOS, Cisco ASA and Cisco FTD) Tj
T*
(1.11 Network connectivity through Cisco ASA and Cisco FTD) Tj
T*
(1.12 Correlation and remediation rules on Cisco FMC) Tj
T*
(2. Secure Connectivity and Segmentation \(20%\)) Tj
T*
(2.1 AnyConnect client-based remote access VPN technologies on Cisco ASA, Cisco FTD, and) Tj
T*
(Cisco Routers.) Tj
T*
(2.2 Cisco IOS CA for VPN authentication) Tj
T*
(2.3 FlexVPN, DMVPN, and IPsec L2L Tunnels) Tj
T*
(2.4 Uplink and downlink MACsec \(802.1AE\)) Tj
T*
(2.5 VPN high availability using) Tj
T*
(2.6 Infrastructure segmentation methods) Tj
T*
(2.7 Micro-segmentation with Cisco TrustSec using SGT and SXP) Tj
T*
(3. Infrastructure Security \(15%\)) Tj
T*
(3.1 Device hardening techniques and control plane protection methods) Tj
T*
(3.2 Management plane protection techniques) Tj
T*
(3.3 Inter Fabric connectivity) Tj
T*
(3.4 Layer 2 security techniques) Tj
T*
